Description: CaramOS Business: manage the company's machines on the LAN
 A company's admin machine manages its employee machines: the wallpaper, the
 Desktop and Documents on the company's server, shared drives, browsers,
 printers, Wi-Fi, required and forbidden apps, a power schedule, USB storage,
 the screen lock, the firewall, shared machines that undo every change at
 reboot, and system snapshots, for the whole company or per department.
 Every feature is off until the admin turns it on.
 .
 It shows an inventory of the machines, an asset list with handover documents,
 health problems, a licence report and a security report, turns help requests
 into tickets, and sends instant actions: lock, a message, restart, shut down,
 update. Remote help starts only after the employee accepts it.
 .
 Employee machines join with a 6-digit code checked without sending it
 (SPAKE2), or in bulk with an enrolment file, also at the first boot of a
 copied disk; the admin may approve each one. They take only the admin's signed
 settings. Nothing covert is collected: no screens, keystrokes, browsing
 history, location or messages.
